    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "BRANIFF\nSystem\nTimetable\nSpring/Summer\n1976\nBraniff gets you there\nwith Flying Colors",
      "BRANIFF\nSERVICE\nHIGHLIGHTS\n• New daily round trip service between Dallas-Fort Worth\nand Washington (National) gives Braniff eight flights every\nbusiness day between the two cities. Six are one-stops\nserving National Airport plus two non-stops serving\nDulles\n• Now two additional flights each way between Denver and\nAtlanta for a total of four every business day.\n• Now four non-stops every business day to\nMinneapolis-St. Paul from Dallas-Fort Worth\n• Other new service from Dallas-Fort Worth includes a\nmidday non-stop to Memphis, afternoon non-stops to\nNashville and New Orleans and additional round trip\nflights serving Seattle-Tacoma and Portland.\n• Ten non-stops every business day between New\nYork-Newark and Dallas-Fort Worth.\n• New afternoon non-stop from Nashville to Dallas-Fort\nWorth makes it a total of three every business day.\n• Every hour service from morning to early evening\nbetween Dallas-Fort Worth and Denver, Chicago,\nHouston and San Antonio.\n• Memphis now has three non-stop round trips every\nbusiness day serving Washington (National).\n• Now morning and evening non-stop service from Kansas\nCity to Houston.\nCheck our schedule for these and other Braniff flights\nthroughout the U.S. Mainland, Hawaii, Mexico and South\nAmerica. Then for reservations call your travel agent or\nBraniff International.\nBRANIFF\nUSMAINLAND HAWAII MEXICO SOUTH AMERICA\n20c2.125. 030,002",
      "airbar\nchoi\nSeattle/Tacon\nPortland/\nMinneapolis/St. Paul\nDes Mo\nOmaha\nKE\nNew York/Newark\nBaltimore/ Washington\nSan Francisco/Oakland\nLos Angeles\nDenver\nColorade\nSprings\nklahor\nAmarillo\nLubbock\nDallas-Fort Wo\nTie\nlashville\nAtlanta,\nOrleans\nHouston\ngrous Christi\nBrownsville\nPerg sourg/Ciparwater/ Tampa\nFi, Lauderdale\nMiami\nawait\nMexico City\nAcapule\nPanama City Ball\nBraniff gets\nyou there with\nFlying Colors\nRio De Janeiro\ninción\nSão Paulo\nSantiag\nBuenos Aires"
